// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Folders and notes - organising a graph
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A folder groups the statements written inside it. Desmos supports one level,
// so folders do not nest. Entries inside a block are comma separated - the
// formatter puts back any comma left out.

config {
    expressionsCollapsed: false
}

"Folders group a long graph into readable sections."

folder "Open by default" {
    "A note inside a folder is an entry like any other.",
    y = sin(x) # color: #c74440,
    y = cos(x) # color: #2d70b3
}

// collapsed on the header starts the folder shut.
folder "Closed by default" { # collapsed: true
    y = sin(2x) # color: #388c46,
    y = cos(2x) # color: #6042a6
}

// A folder can hold the working parts of a construction, hidden away.
folder "Working values" { # collapsed: true
    amp = 2 # sliderBounds: {min: 0, max: 5, step: 0.1},
    freq = 3 # sliderBounds: {min: 1, max: 8, step: 1}
}

"Anything after the closing brace is back at the top level."

y = amp * sin(freq * x) # color: #fa7e19, lineWidth: 3
